Dispatch's answers to the daemon's status writes, which client_test.go serves from an httptest
server to HTTPClient.ChangeStatus and HTTPClient.SetStatusAt, one case for each file here.

A file comes in one of two forms:

  <name>.http                       one whole answer as `curl --include` prints it: the status
                                    line, every header and the body, with CRLF line ends.
  <name>_<status>.handwritten.json  the JSON body of an answer no Dispatch served yet, its HTTP
                                    status the number that ends its name. It is written by hand
                                    from the status-change route's interface (INFRA-4731, as the
                                    plan of INFRA-4730 gives it in "The interfaces this work
                                    depends on"), each issue in it in the shape of a captured PATCH
                                    answer (key_replayed.http). A capture from a Dispatch that
                                    serves the route replaces each, and the file it leaves holds
                                    what the route really answers.

Captured on 2026-11-20 between 15:47:21Z and 15:47:57Z from `bun run dispatch:local`
(packages/dispatch/e2e/local-instance.ts), built from this repository at commit 25c0b17968b3,
whose Dispatch serves no status-change route. It ran with DATABASE_URL naming a new database of
its own, and the commands below use the URL it printed as $URL, its agent token e2e-token and the
issues its seed files (CORE-1 to CORE-7). Each command writes the file named beside it:

  status_change_no_route.http  the router's 404 of a Dispatch older than the route, which the
                               client reads as NoRoute:
      curl -sS --include -X POST -H 'Accept: application/json' -H 'Authorization: Bearer e2e-token' \
        -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -H 'Idempotency-Key: capture-no-route-1' \
        "$URL/api/v1/issues/CORE-1/status-change" \
        -d '{"status":"backlog","unlink_children":true,"actor":{"kind":"session","id":"legion-daemon:CORE"}}'

The request key's answers are the same on every POST and PATCH route (keyedWrites in
packages/envoy/internal/dispatch/api/request_keys.go), so these were captured on the issue PATCH.
Each command below sends, besides the Idempotency-Key it names, the headers of the first one:
Accept: application/json, Authorization: Bearer e2e-token and Content-Type: application/json.

  key_reused.http     422 KEY_REUSED: a second PATCH under one key with another body; the first,
                      under the same key, was answered 200.
      curl -sS --include -X PATCH ... -H 'Idempotency-Key: capture-key-reused-1' "$URL/api/v1/issues/CORE-4" \
        -d '{"status":"backlog","actor":{"kind":"session","id":"legion-daemon:CORE"}}'
      curl -sS --include -X PATCH ... -H 'Idempotency-Key: capture-key-reused-1' "$URL/api/v1/issues/CORE-4" \
        -d '{"status":"todo","actor":{"kind":"session","id":"legion-daemon:CORE"}}'

  key_replayed.http   the repeat of a finished PATCH under its key: the first answer's status and
                      body again, with Idempotency-Replayed: ?1. The same command was run twice;
                      this is the second answer, whose body is byte for byte the first's.
      curl -sS --include -X PATCH ... -H 'Idempotency-Key: capture-key-replayed-1' "$URL/api/v1/issues/CORE-5" \
        -d '{"status":"todo","expected_sequence":3,"actor":{"kind":"session","id":"legion-daemon:CORE"}}'

  key_in_flight.http  409 KEY_IN_FLIGHT with Retry-After: 1: the repeat of a PATCH whose first run
                      still runs. Dispatch's slow-write hook (DISPATCH_TEST_HOOKS=1, which
                      dispatch:local sets; slow_write_hook.go) holds the first run five seconds,
                      and the repeat is sent one second after it:
      curl -sS ... -X POST "$URL/api/v1/writes/_test/slow" \
        -d '{"method":"PATCH","path":"/api/v1/issues/CORE-7","delay_ms":5000}'
      curl -sS --include -X PATCH ... -H 'Idempotency-Key: capture-key-in-flight-1' "$URL/api/v1/issues/CORE-7" \
        -d '{"status":"backlog","actor":{"kind":"session","id":"legion-daemon:CORE"}}' &
      sleep 1
      (the same PATCH again, in the foreground: this answer)
      curl -sS ... -X POST "$URL/api/v1/writes/_test/slow" \
        -d '{"method":"PATCH","path":"/api/v1/issues/CORE-7","delay_ms":0}'

  key_committed.http  409 KEY_COMMITTED: the repeat of a write that committed and kept no answer.
                      The agent-token mint is the route that answers so on demand
                      (answerHoldsSecret in request_keys.go: its answer holds a secret, so its key
                      keeps none), and it takes a person, here alice by dev sign-in. The first
                      answer, 201 with the new token, was not kept:
      curl -sS -o /dev/null -c jar "$URL/auth/_dev/signin?login=alice&next=/"
      curl -sS -o /dev/null -X POST -b jar -H "Origin: $URL" -H 'Accept: application/json' \
        -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -H 'Idempotency-Key: capture-key-committed-1' \
        "$URL/api/v1/me/agent-tokens" -d '{"name":"capture-key-committed"}'
      (the same POST again, with --include in place of -o /dev/null: this answer)

Hand-written, each the answer to a call on LEGION-1, a parent at work with LEGION-2 (and, in the
midway refusal, LEGION-3) at work under it:

  status_change_include_children_200.handwritten.json
                      backlog with include_children, fenced at 7: LEGION-2's step, then LEGION-1's.
  status_change_dry_run_200.handwritten.json
                      the same call with dry_run: the entries it would make, no issue in them.
  status_change_stale_sequence_409.handwritten.json
                      the same call fenced at a stale sequence: 409 ISSUE_CHANGED, nothing changed.
  status_change_no_option_409.handwritten.json
                      backlog with no option: 409 PARENT_STATUS_CONFLICT naming LEGION-2.
  status_change_midway_refused_409.handwritten.json
                      backlog with include_children while a person writes LEGION-1 between two
                      steps: 409 ISSUE_CHANGED with the entry of the step that committed.

Once INFRA-4731's route is merged in, the first four are captured from `bun run dispatch:local`
run with DISPATCH_PARENT_STATUS_RULE=on (and again off) on a seeded parent with an open child,
one `curl --include` of the route per answer into status_change_<case>.http, and the midway
refusal and the keyed repeat of a run that stopped by TestCaptureStatusChangeAnswers
(internal/daemon/status_change_capture_test.go, build tag capture, run by hand):

  go -C packages/daemon test -tags capture -count=1 -run '^TestCaptureStatusChangeAnswers$' ./internal/daemon/

which writes status_change_midway_refused.http and status_change_keyed_repeat.http here. Each
capture then takes the place of the hand-written file of its case, and client_test.go's case
names the capture.
